From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco Vitale <mrcvtl@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:41:18 +0000
Subject: [maglev] Preserve number checks when untagging HoleyFloat64

When MaglevGraphOptimizer unwraps a ReturnedValue or
HoleyFloat64ToTagged node into a HoleyFloat64 input for a
TruncateCheckedNumberOrOddballToInt32 assuming kNumber,
GetTruncatedInt32ForToNumber ignores assumed_input_type and emits an
unchecked TruncateHoleyFloat64ToInt32. This drops the runtime check that
deopts on holes and undefined, allowing undefined to reach downstream
operations that rely on the kNumber type.

This CL converts HoleyFloat64 inputs to Float64 via
GetFloat64ForToNumber whenever the assumed input type forbids undefined,
emitting a CheckedHoleyFloat64ToFloat64 guard before truncation. It also
checks CanReuseAlternative when matching the target representation
directly.

Fixed: 568348290
Change-Id: Ib5e66da49503a74a4ded7526ad95d9166a6a6964
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8525046
Auto-Submit: Marco Vitale <mrcvtl@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Darius Mercadier <dmercadier@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Marco Vitale <mrcvtl@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#110613}

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y):
Applied on top of the adapted c713c92ce08f: the new CanReuseAlternative()
check and the HoleyFloat64 guard use the assumed_input_type derived from this
branch's conversion_type parameter (see that patch). The eager-deopt guard on
this branch is current_node_->properties().has_eager_deopt_info() rather than
CanEagerDeopt(); the inserted block is placed directly after it, as upstream.

diff --git a/src/maglev/maglev-graph-optimizer.cc b/src/maglev/maglev-graph-optimizer.cc
index 69cdad7d185453173231d4000a83358257d108a2..3c2e09da4513c28d2c22a5d86e1c17031374c3f9 100644
--- a/src/maglev/maglev-graph-optimizer.cc
+++ b/src/maglev/maglev-graph-optimizer.cc
@@ -628,7 +628,8 @@ MaybeReduceResult MaglevGraphOptimizer::GetUntaggedValueWithRepresentation(
   if (conversion_type.has_value()) {
     assumed_input_type = GetAllowedTypeFromConversionType(*conversion_type);
   }
-  if (node->value_representation() == ValueRepresentationFromUse(use_repr)) {
+  if (node->value_representation() == ValueRepresentationFromUse(use_repr) &&
+      CanReuseAlternative(node, node, use_repr, assumed_input_type)) {
     return node;
   }
   if (node->Is<ReturnedValue>()) {
@@ -658,6 +659,15 @@ MaybeReduceResult MaglevGraphOptimizer::GetUntaggedValueWithRepresentation(
   if (!current_node_->properties().has_eager_deopt_info()) {
     return {};
   }
+  if (node->is_holey_float64() && assumed_input_type.has_value() &&
+      NodeTypeIs(*assumed_input_type, NodeType::kNumberOrBoolean)) {
+    // HoleyFloat64 can hold the hole or undefined, whereas the replaced node
+    // checked that the input is a number (or boolean, which cannot occur in
+    // HoleyFloat64). Convert to Float64 first so CheckedHoleyFloat64ToFloat64
+    // preserves the check that subsequent operations may rely on.
+    GET_VALUE_OR_ABORT(
+        node, reducer_.GetFloat64ForToNumber(node, *assumed_input_type));
+  }
   switch (use_repr) {
     case UseRepresentation::kInt32:
       return reducer_.GetInt32(node);
diff --git a/test/mjsunit/turbolev/regress-568348290.js b/test/mjsunit/turbolev/regress-568348290.js
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2f39a98cc33c361f9af211899325d8c9b56a3337
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/mjsunit/turbolev/regress-568348290.js
@@ -0,0 +1,149 @@
+// Copyright 2026 the V8 project authors. All rights reserved.
